{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L164-L194","doc":"**Full single-generator character `χ_λ(σ) = c_λ·h` (all three tableau\nclasses).** The seminormal character of `σ` on `S^λ` splits the standard\ntableaux into three classes by where `1, 2` sit: **same-row** (diagonal\neigenvalue `q`), **same-column** (diagonal eigenvalue `−q⁻¹`), and\n**off-diagonal** (weight `a_ρ`). The two Hecke eigenvalues satisfy\n`q + (−q⁻¹) = q − q⁻¹ = h`, so the same-column eigenvalue is `−q⁻¹ = h − q`\n(stated that way here to keep the identity inverse-free). For a\n**self-conjugate** `λ` the same-row and same-column counts are equal\n(`Rrow.card = Rcol.card`, conjugation symmetry), so the diagonal contribution\n`r·q + r·(h − q) = r·h` is an integer multiple of `h`; the off-diagonal part is\n`(|Soff|/2)·h` by `two_mul_characterSum_eq`. Hence\n\n  2·χ_λ(σ) = (2·|Rrow| + |Soff|)·h,   i.e.  χ_λ(σ) = c_λ·h,  c_λ = |Rrow| + |Soff|/2 ∈ ℤ.\n\nThis is the complete abstract form of `symbolic_character_table` — sorry-free,\nreducing that block to supplying the concrete tableau partition + the swap\ninvolution `τ` on the off-diagonal class (bean `qou-9vvr` / `qou-tqab`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.two_mul_characterSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.two_mul_characterSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L150-L162","doc":"**`2·χ_λ(σ) = |S|·h` — the general closed form `χ_λ(σ) = c_λ·h`, `c_λ = |S|/2`.**\nThe single-generator seminormal character over a standard-tableau set `S`\ncarrying the `i ↔ i+1` swap involution is `c_λ·h` with `c_λ = |S|/2 ∈ ℤ`.\nComposes `characterSum_eq_h_mul` (h factors out) with `two_mul_reducedSum_eq_card`\n(the reduced sum is the integer `|S|/2`). No `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.two_mul_reducedSum_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.two_mul_reducedSum_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L113-L148","doc":"**The reduced-weight sum is `|S|/2` — the integer content `c_λ` (general).**\nIf the SYT index set `S` carries a fixed-point-free involution `τ` that negates\nthe axial distance (`ρ(τ t) = −ρ t` — the `i ↔ i+1` transposition swapping the\ntwo boxes, which negates `ρ` by `TableauContent.axialDistance_antisymm`), then\n`2·Σ_t g_{ρ(t)} = |S|`: each τ-pair contributes `g_ρ + g_{−ρ} = 1`, so the sum\nis the pair count `|S|/2 ∈ ℤ`. The proof reindexes `∑ g_{−ρ t}` by `τ` (via\n`Finset.sum_image` over the involution) into `∑ g_{ρ t}`, then applies the\npairing identity termwise. This is the **integer content** `c_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.characterSum_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.characterSum_pair","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**`χ_λ(σ) = c_λ · h` end-to-end for a two-tableau partition (`c_λ = 1`).**\nComposes `characterSum_eq_h_mul` (h factors out) with `reducedSum_pair`\n(the reduced sum is the integer `1`): the single-generator seminormal character\nover a one-pair SYT set is exactly `h`. This is the full closed form realised on\nthe base case — the weight + geometry layers deliver `χ = c_λ·h` with no\noutstanding `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedSum_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedSum_pair","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**Integer content `c_λ = 1` — the two-tableau base case.** When the SYT set is\na single swap-pair `{a, b}` with `ρ(b) = −ρ(a)` (one off-diagonal box pair, the\nboxes exchanged by the `i ↔ i+1` transposition), the reduced-weight sum is `1`.\nThe base case of `Σ g_ρ = c_λ ∈ ℤ`, provable directly from the pairing identity\n(no general involution reindex). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight_add_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight_add_neg","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L63-L89","doc":"**The pairing identity** `g_ρ + g_{−ρ} = 1`.\n\nWith `x = q^{2ρ}`: `g_ρ = (1 − x⁻¹)⁻¹ = x/(x−1)` and `g_{−ρ} = (1 − x)⁻¹ =\n−1/(x−1)`, so the sum telescopes to `1`. This is *why* a reduced-weight sum\nover a ρ ↔ −ρ symmetric standard-tableau set is an **integer** `c_λ`: the\noff-diagonal boxes pair up, each pair contributing `1`. Hypotheses: `q ≠ 0`\n(so `zpow` inverts) and `q^{2ρ} ≠ 1` (so no box sits on the diagonal, i.e.\n`i, i+1` are neither same-row nor same-column). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L57-L61","doc":"Rewriting `q^{−2ρ}` as `(q^{2ρ})⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.characterSum_eq_h_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.characterSum_eq_h_mul","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L46-L55","doc":"**Character sum factors out `h`.** The single-generator seminormal character\nis a sum of weights `Σ_{t ∈ S} a_{ρ(t)}` over the standard-tableau index set\n`S`; `h` pulls out of the whole sum: `χ_λ(σ) = h · Σ_t g_{ρ(t)}`. Together with\n`Σ_t g_{ρ(t)} = c_λ ∈ ℤ` (the reduced-weight sum over the swap-symmetric SYT\nset — an integer by the pairing identity `reducedWeight_add_neg`) this is the\nclosed form `χ_λ(σ) = c_λ · h`. The `h`-linearity of the whole table is thus\nreduced to a purely *integer* combinatorial statement about the reduced sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.seminormalWeight_eq_h_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.seminormalWeight_eq_h_mul","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L40-L44","doc":"**The `h` factors out.** `a_ρ = h · g_ρ`. This is the algebraic source of the\n`· h` in the character closed form `χ_λ(σ) = c_λ · h`: every summand carries a\nsingle factor of `h`, so the whole character does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.seminormalWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.seminormalWeight","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L36-L38","doc":"**Seminormal weight** `a_ρ = h / (1 − q^{−2ρ})`, `h = q − q⁻¹` the Hecke\nparameter (AGENTS.md §7a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight.reducedWeight","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalWeight.lean#L31-L34","doc":"**Reduced seminormal weight** `g_ρ = 1/(1 − q^{−2ρ})` — the dimensionless part\nof the axial-distance weight, `ρ : ℤ` the axial distance between the boxes\nholding `i` and `i+1` in a standard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0}]}